QUESTION NUMBER 4

Starvation Debugging 
Root cause of starvation:
P5 is placed in the lowest-priority queue .
Higher-priority queuescontinuously receive processes.
Scheduler always serves higher-priority queues first.
P5 never gets CPU time.
This results in starvation.
Optimization to ensure fairness:
Implement aging to gradually increase P5's priority.
Allocate CPU time periodically to lower-priority queues.
Use a fair scheduling policy to prevent starvation.

QUESTION NUMBER 5

 Context-Switch Overhead Debugging 
Reason for high context switching:
Scheduler performs 20,000 context switches per second.
Time quantum is very small 
Threads have an average burst time of 2 ms.
Frequent I/O waits trigger additional context switches.
Excessive switching increases CPU overhead and reduces performance.
Optimizations:
Increase the time quantum to reduce unnecessary context switches.
Reduce I/O blocking using asynchronous I/O or I/O buffering.
Optimize scheduling to minimize frequent preemption.
